      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    initial_dividend = 0.22\n    high_growth_rate = 0.12\n    stable_growth_rate = 0.06\n    required_return = 0.09\n    high_growth_years = 4\n\n    # Calculate dividend at the end of the high-growth period\n    dividend_year_4 = initial_dividend * (1 + high_growth_rate) ** high_growth_years\n\n    # Calculate the dividend in the first stable-growth year\n    dividend_year_5 = dividend_year_4 * (1 + stable_growth_rate)\n\n    # Calculate terminal value at the end of year 4 using the Gordon Growth Model\n    terminal_value = dividend_year_5 / (required_return - stable_growth_rate)\n\n    # Return the answer rounded to three decimal places\n    return round(terminal_value, 3)\n```",
